\': \'client\'}, {\'name\': \'tcp.connect\', \'spanKind\': \'internal\'}, {\'name\': \'HTTP GET /hotels\', \'spanKind\': \'server\'}, {\'name\': \'oteldemo.CartService/AddItem\', \'spanKind\': \'client\'}, {\'name\': \'GET /api/products/{productId}\', \'spanKind\': \'server\'}, {\'name\': \'/search.Search/Nearby\', \'spanKind\': \'client\'}, {\'name\': \'oteldemo.CheckoutService/PlaceOrder\', \'spanKind\': \'client\'}, {\'name\': \'executing api route (pages) /api/recommendations\', \'spanKind\': \'internal\'}]", annotations=None)] isError=False', id='74a98127-a48b-4346-abb8-9dac1f15674e', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-a625b8e6d09fed70'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='5348f0c6-3b05-4cf0-97a2-47f80d629ec0'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s see. The user is trying to diagnose issues in the OpenTelemetry Demo Astronomy Shop application. So far, they checked the pods and deployments, and everything seems to be running normally. The frontend service had a restart, but the deployments are all healthy. Then they looked into the frontend\'s operations and found a list of API routes and service calls.\n\nNow, the next step is to figure out why the frontend service restarted. Since the operations list shows various API routes and service interactions, maybe there\'s an error in one of those calls. The user needs to check the traces for the frontend service to see if there are any errors or anomalies in the distributed transactions. \n\nThe get_traces tool can retrieve Jaeger traces for the frontend service. By looking at the traces, they can identify if any specific operation is failing, causing the frontend to crash or restart. They should check for errors, timeouts, or failed dependencies in the traces. If a particular service call is problematic, that could be the root cause. \n\nSo, using get_traces with a reasonable time frame, like the last 5 minutes, would help capture any recent issues. This will allow them to pinpoint the exact operation or service that\'s causing the frontend to fail, leading to the restart. Once they find the faulty service or operation, they can then investigate further into that specific component.\n</think>\n\nget_traces  \nThe frontend service had a recent restart, and its operations list shows multiple API routes and service calls. To identify the root cause, I need to examine the traces for the frontend service to detect errors, failed requests, or anomalies in its distributed transactions. This will help pinpoint if a specific operation or dependency is causing the instability.  \n\n<tool_call>\n{"name": "get_traces", "arguments": {"service": "frontend", "last_n_minutes": 5}}\n</tool_call>', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=380, prompt_tokens=4458, total_tokens=4838, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc11-6ee6-7e12-ad2a-9f962c92e00f-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 4458, 'output_tokens': 380, 'total_tokens': 4838}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='9f966420-92e4-47af-a2f3-6c9fcf7803b4')]]
