9a', 'operationName': 'postgresql', 'references': [{'refType': 'CHILD_OF', 'traceID': '757ed8e93f04e16e51cf639eec85c242', 'spanID': 'b9c727dc7c8ca560'}], 'startTime': 1773755519990430, 'duration': 792, 'tags': [{'key': 'db.system.name', 'type': 'string', 'value': 'postgresql'}, {'key': 'db.query.text', 'type': 'string', 'value': '\\n\\t\\tSELECT p.id, p.name, p.description, p.picture, \\n\\t\\t       p.price_currency_code, p.price_units, p.price_nanos, p.categories\\n\\t\\tFROM catalog.products p\\n\\t\\tWHERE p.id = $1\\n\\t'}, {'key': 'unsanitized_span_name', 'type': 'string', 'value': 'sql.conn.query'}, {'key': 'span.kind', 'type': 'string', 'value': 'client'}, {'key': 'internal.span.format', 'type': 'string', 'value': 'otlp'}], 'logs': [], 'processID': 'p7', 'warnings': None}, {'traceID': '757ed8e93f04e16e51cf639eec85c242', 'spanID': 'b9c727dc7c8ca560', 'operationName': 'oteldemo.ProductCatalogService/GetProduct', 'references': [{'refType': 'CHILD_OF', 'traceID': '757ed8e93f04e16e51cf639eec85c242', 'spanID': '1b4b1dd47abc4af9'}], 'startTime': 1773755519990367, 'duration': 941, 'tags': [{'key': 'rpc", id='0ff81435-a21f-4457-801e-dc76cbcddc1a', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-84c554dcb1e9bf40'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='bc7077d1-709e-418c-94ae-13a35a9bd9c7'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s see. The user is trying to diagnose an issue with the OpenTelemetry Demo Astronomy Shop application. So far, they\'ve checked the pods and deployments, and everything seems to be running normally. The frontend service had a restart, but the pods are up and running. Then they looked into the frontend\'s operations and traces.\n\nLooking at the traces, most of them have a 200 status code, which is good. But there are some warnings, like clock skew adjustments being disabled. However, the main issue here is that the frontend service restarted once. The user wants to find the root cause of any faults.\n\nWait, the user mentioned that some or none of the microservices have faults. The initial checks didn\'t show any obvious issues. The traces don\'t show errors, but maybe there\'s a deeper problem. The frontend\'s restart could be a symptom. Maybe there\'s a dependency issue or a configuration problem.\n\nThe traces include calls to services like cart, product-catalog, and others. Let me check if any of those services have issues. For example, the trace for \'oteldemo.ProductCatalogService/GetProduct\' shows a successful response. The \'postgresql\' span also seems okay. But maybe there\'s a latency issue or a failed request that\'s not captured here.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the frontend\'s restart was due to a configuration error or a resource issue. The user could check the logs of the frontend pod to see why it restarted. But the available tools don\'t include log retrieval directly. Wait, there\'s the \'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd\' tool which can run \'kubectl logs\' to get pod logs. That might be necessary to find out why the frontend restarted.\n\nBut the user hasn\'t checked the logs yet. Since the traces don\'t show errors, the next step would be to look into the logs of the frontend pod to identify any exceptions or errors that caused the restart. So, using the \'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd\' with \'kubectl logs\' on the frontend pod would be the next logical step. That way, they can see if there\'s an underlying issue like a crash or configuration mistake.\n</think>\n\nexec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \nTo investigate the frontend service\'s restart, I need to examine its logs for errors, crashes, or configuration issues that may have caused the restart. This tool will execute `kubectl logs frontend-55df67b4b9-k9rmj -n astronomy-shop` to retrieve the pod\'s logs and identify the root cause of the restart.  \n\n<tool_call>\n{"name": "exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd", "arguments": {"command": "kubectl logs frontend-55df67b4b9-k9rmj -n astronomy-shop"}}\n</tool_call>', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 565, 'prompt_tokens': 11444, 'total_tokens': 12009, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc11-c240-7e32-b94e-f0a77b954cb2-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 11444, 'output_tokens': 565, 'total_tokens': 12009}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='e10b53e8-d277-473f-b9b3-0eca04985116'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s see. The user is trying to diagnose an issue with the frontend service in the astronomy-shop namespace. Earlier steps showed that the frontend pod had a restart, and the traces didn\'t show any errors. Now, the user is asking to check the logs of the frontend pod to find out why it restarted.\n\nFirst, I need to confirm which pod is the frontend pod. From the previous kubectl get pods output, the frontend pod is named frontend-55df67b4b9-k9rmj. The user already used exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd to get the logs, but the response seems cut off. The tool_response provided ends with the command "kubectl logs frontend-55df67b4b9-k9rmj -n astronomy-shop" and then the content is incomplete, ending with "oteldemo.ProductCatalogService/GetProduct", which is part of a trace.\n\nWait, maybe the logs were not fully retrieved. The user might need to run the logs command again to get the full log output. However, in the current setup, the tool call is already made, and the response is partial. The assistant needs to check if the logs contain any error messages or exceptions that caused the restart. Since the provided logs don\'t show any obvious errors, the next step would be to look into the deployment configuration or check for resource limits. But according to the tools available, the next step would be to use another tool if needed. However, the user has already used the exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd to get the logs. \n\nSince the logs didn\'t show any errors, maybe the issue is elsewhere. The user might need to check the deployment\'s rollout history or check for any configuration issues. But given the tools available, the next step would be to submit the answer based on the current information. The root cause might be a transient issue that\'s not logged, or maybe a configuration problem. However, since the logs don\'t show errors, the assistant should conclude that the frontend service restarted but no specific error was found in the logs, and perhaps check other components like the deployment or resource limits. But since the tools don\'t include checking deployment rollouts or resource usage beyond kubectl, the answer might be that no faults were found in the logs, and the issue might be elsewhere. However, the user\'s instructions say to stop diagnosis once the root cause is found. Since no errors were found in the logs, maybe the answer is that no faults were detected.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl logs frontend-55df67b4b9-k9rmj -n astronomy-shop"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-89c083a8950fc3d3', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 557, 'prompt_tokens': 12471, 'total_tokens': 13028, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc11-e0ee-7632-9041-cf663ce27a03-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl logs frontend-55df67b4b9-k9rmj -n astronomy-shop'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-89c083a8950fc3d3', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 12471, 'output_tokens': 557, 'total_tokens': 13028}), ToolMessage(content='▲ Next.js 16.1.1\n- Local:         http://frontend-55df67b4b9-k9rmj:8080\n- Network:       http://frontend-55df67b4b9-k9rmj:8080\n\n✓ Starting...\n✓ Ready in 177ms\n', id='ebc6d05e-c7cb-4afe-aeed-ba49af3d298d', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-89c083a8950fc3d3'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='5f5973f9-8da7-43e7-b1d9-56250c644dcf')]]
