e, like the last 5 minutes, would help capture any recent issues. This will allow them to pinpoint the exact operation or service that\'s causing the frontend to fail, leading to the restart. Once they find the faulty service or operation, they can then investigate further into that specific component.\n</think>\n\nget_traces  \nThe frontend service had a recent restart, and its operations list shows multiple API routes and service calls. To identify the root cause, I need to examine the traces for the frontend service to detect errors, failed requests, or anomalies in its distributed transactions. This will help pinpoint if a specific operation or dependency is causing the instability.  \n\n<tool_call>\n{"name": "get_traces", "arguments": {"service": "frontend", "last_n_minutes": 5}}\n</tool_call>', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 380, 'prompt_tokens': 4458, 'total_tokens': 4838, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc11-6ee6-7e12-ad2a-9f962c92e00f-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 4458, 'output_tokens': 380, 'total_tokens': 4838}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='9f966420-92e4-47af-a2f3-6c9fcf7803b4'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let's see. The user is trying to diagnose an issue with the OpenTelemetry Demo Astronomy Shop application. They've already checked the pods and deployments, and everything seems to be running. The frontend service had a restart, so they looked into its operations and found various API routes and service calls. Now, they're using the get_traces tool to check for any issues in the frontend's traces.\n\nThe last tool call was get_t