f88b97'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let's see. The user is trying to diagnose why the frontend service in the OpenTelemetry Demo Astronomy Shop is restarting. So far, they checked the pods and deployments, looked at the frontend's operations, traces, and logs. The frontend pod has a CrashLoopBackOff status with 4 restarts. The logs show the pod started and was ready, but then it crashed. The liveness probe is failing with a 404 error.\n\nHmm, the liveness probe is set to check /healthz, which isn't found. That means the application isn't serving that endpoint. Maybe the app isn't running correctly, or the endpoint is misconfigured. The user needs to check the application's health endpoint. \n\nLooking at the environment variables, the frontend is using several service addresses like ad, cart, checkout, etc. Maybe one of those services is down, causing the frontend to fail. But the traces showed some calls to cart and product-catalog, which were successful. Wait, but the liveness probe is failing. \n\nAlternatively, the application might not be starting properly. The logs only show the initial startup, no errors. Maybe the liveness probe is misconfigured. The probe is checking http://:8080/healthz, but the app might be serving on a different path or the endpoint is incorrect. \n\nThe user should check the liveness probe configuration. Maybe the path is wrong. Also, looking at the container's command or entrypoint, perhaps the app isn't starting correctly. But the logs don't show any errors. \n\nAnother angle: the frontend might be dependent on other services. If any of those services are down, it could cause the frontend to fail. But the traces from the last 5 minutes show some successful calls. However, the liveness probe is failing, which is a Kubernetes-level check, not directly related to the services. \n\nWait, the liveness probe failure is causing the pod to restart. So the root cause is the liveness probe failing. The user needs to check why the /healthz endpoint isn't responding. Maybe the app isn't running, or the endpoint is incorrect. \n\nSince the user can't run more commands, they should submit the root cause based on the available info. The liveness probe is failing because the /healthz endpoint isn't available, leading to restarts. The frontend service might not be properly configured to serve that endpoint, or the application isn't running as expected.\n</think>\n\nsubmit_tool  \nThe frontend service is experiencing repeated restarts due to a failing liveness probe. The liveness probe checks the `/healthz` endpoint, which is returning a 404 error, indicating the application is not serving this endpoint. This suggests either:  \n1. The application is not running correctly (e.g., misconfigured or crashed immediately after startup).  \n2. The health endpoint path (`/healthz`) is incorrect or the application is not exposing it.  \n3. Dependencies (e.g., `cart`, `product-catalog`, or other services) are unreachable, causing the frontend to fail silently.  \n\nThe root cause is the liveness probe failure, which triggers restarts. Further investigation into the application's health endpoint configuration and dependency availability is required.", additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=669, prompt_tokens=13325, total_tokens=13994, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc12-59b5-7fd3-aab9-0d7f126bf845-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 13325, 'output_tokens': 669, 'total_tokens': 13994}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='d5e5ab0e-b3e9-40f1-a907-0db7a3fff9ef')]]
