ess probe settings is the next best step. So, the tool call should be to get the deployment\'s YAML to inspect the probe configuration.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_kubectl_cmd_safely\n\nReasoning: The logs show the frontend application started but the liveness probe still fails. This suggests the `/healthz` endpoint may not be properly configured or exposed. We need to inspect the deployment configuration to verify the liveness probe settings and ensure the endpoint is correctly defined in the application.\n\ntool_call: {"command": "kubectl get deployment frontend -n astronomy-shop -o yaml"}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=344, prompt_tokens=3583, total_tokens=3927, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc13-151c-7981-ba66-8bdc85193230-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 3583, 'output_tokens': 344, 'total_tokens': 3927}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='2d3ff670-063c-4a14-b01a-3ea28b5364b0')]]
